# An animated Inkmoth Nexus is a creature, so Clone may choose it, but the animation is an effect and not a copiable
# value (CR 707.2): the Clone is an Inkmoth Nexus that is a Land and nothing else - not an artifact, not a creature, no
# Phyrexian or Blinkmoth, no flying or infect - so it does not die as a 0/0. On turn 1 Bot1 taps its Inkmoth Nexus for
# {C} and spends it animating the Nexus, then casts Clone with Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire. The original is still a
# 1/1 artifact creature land, and the Clone was not played as a land.

[Bot1 Deck]
Inkmoth Nexus
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Clone
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Inkmoth Nexus.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus.Activate(Ability: {T})
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus.Activate(Ability: {1})
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Inkmoth Nexus; Inkmoth Nexus; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus#1.Types = Land; Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus#1.Keywords = Flying; Infect
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus#2.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus#2.Subtypes = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Inkmoth Nexus#2.Keywords = (absent)
